  message: "ADR-0051 annotation (WI-virav; annotate only -- no fold, no closure, no re-prioritisation). CLAUSE VIOLATED: owner path \"spelled in the source language's import vocabulary\". NOTION THE SLOT CARRIES: namespace -- the WRONG one: the slot holds the parent package (`defusedcsv`) and the submodule that actually owns the symbol (`defusedcsv.csv`) sits in the NAME slot. Pair 3 shape (qualifier in the NAME slot) with the owner path truncated one segment short, which is why neither catalogue spelling can match it."  # b3a3
- op: discuss  # 9146
  at: '2026-09-28T08:48:51Z'  # 9146
  by: agent  # 9146
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9146
  clock: 4  # 9146
  nonce: '9146'  # 9146
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-28 at dev 5f80a79081. PREMISE HOLDS; THE CONSEQUENCE IS UNDERSTATED. This is a FALSE ALL-CLEAR on verify-claims, not only a blocked catalogue addition. Record: scratchpad sugom/ (run*.py, census.py).\n\nEMISSION, unchanged: py.py:8336 (the 'imported_name.method()' arm of _process_call) emits python:{module}:0-0:{original_name}.{attr}. symbol_imports maps 'from P import X' to (P, X) at py.py:2516, so the owner's last segment lands in the NAME slot.\n\nSHIPPED COMMAND, must_not_exist claim per case (the control is the same call spelled with a plain import):\n  from urllib import request; request.urlopen(u)        net_send  CONFIRMED, 0 caveats  (control: violated)\n  from xml.etree import ElementTree; ElementTree.parse  fs_read   CONFIRMED  (control: violated)\n  from xml.dom import minidom; minidom.parse(p)         fs_read   CONFIRMED\n  from importlib import resources; resources.read_text  fs_read   CONFIRMED\n  from importlib import metadata; metadata.version('x') fs_read   CONFIRMED\n  from os import path; path.exists(p)                   fs_read   CONFIRMED  (control: violated)\nCaught today: os.environ.get / sys.stdin.read / sys.stdout.write, and only because their rows are ATTRIBUTE rows that the file-level import edge matches (INV-lagir). Also caught: datetime.now(), and only by COINCIDENCE: INV-januj's strip_redundant_module_qualifier retry (io_boundary.py ~4980) drops a qualifier that REPEATS the module (datetime + datetime.now -> now), and the class happens to share its module's name. date.today() is not caught.\n\nTWO DOORS, and a fix must close both:\n (a) MATCHER MISS: the rowed member is never classified (the cases above).\n (b) THE COVERAGE GATE VOUCHES THE PARENT'S GRANT FOR AN UNAUDITED SUBMODULE. _adjudicate_external_modules step (2) asks module_io_is_enumerated on the module slot, 'urllib' (granted 2026-08-15) instead of 'urllib.request'. python.yaml's grant header forbids exactly this (\"declaring urllib does NOT vouch for urllib.request\"). Measured with UNROWED members:\n      from logging import handlers; handlers.RotatingFileHandler(p)  fs_write CONFIRMED   (import logging.handlers form: inconclusive)\n      from xml import sax; sax.parse(p, h)                           fs_read  CONFIRMED   (import xml.sax form: inconclusive)\n   A matcher-side retry (split X.y into module P.X, name y) closes (a) only. Emitting module P.X, name y at py.py:8336 closes both, and is the spelling the control forms already produce (urllib.request:urlopen, pathlib.Path:home).\n\nSCOPE, a SOURCE census (not the instrument; ast over ~/all_repos_first_party_py.txt, 54,567 files): 'from P import X' then 'X.attr(...)' where P is granted and (P.X, attr) is a catalogued row = 2,458 sites in 70 repos. Excluding the spellings caught above (datetime.datetime by coincidence; os.environ, sys.stdin, sys.stdout as attributes), about 460 sites across 11 owners are misses: pathlib.Path 238 (cwd 160, home 48), datetime.date 119, os.path 31, importlib.metadata 31, importlib.resources 16, urllib.request 11, xml.etree.ElementTree 8, ctypes.cdll 5, plus 4 more. Door (b) sites (unrowed member, unaudited submodule) were NOT counted.\n\nSTILL TRUE: the catalogue convention. Python now carries 0 dotted names (the description's '1 of 1979' was across all languages at the time), so a dotted-name row remains the wrong cure.\n\nRELATED, NOT MERGED: WI-torin (P3) is the CLASS half of this same emission (date.today, Path.cwd, ctypes.cdll.LoadLibrary): the one py.py line, the same false confirmed. Surfaced as a fold candidate, not folded. Priority NOT changed (owner's call): this row is P2 and WI-torin P3, while both produce a clean confirmed verdict."  # 9146
